UniKey Vietnamese engine — LGPLv2 §6 compliance for colorburst
==============================================================

What this is
------------
The files in /usr/share/unikey-engine-source/ are the complete source of the
UniKey Vietnamese input engine ("ukengine", LGPL-2.0-or-later) as vendored into
this build, INCLUDING colorburst's modifications:

  * ukengine.cpp/.h, inputproc.cpp/.h  — the upstream LGPL engine core, unmodified
  * keycons.h, vnlexi.h, mactab.h      — upstream headers
  * charset.h, charset_utf8.cpp,
    vnlexi_tables.cpp, gen_tables.py    — colorburst's clean-room replacement for
                                          the engine's GPL-charset coupling (a
                                          UTF-8 emitter + regenerated code-point
                                          tables); LGPL, not a license severance
  * mactab_stub.cpp                     — macro table stubbed out (gõ tắt off)
  * BUILD.gn                            — how it is compiled into ash-chrome
  * README.chromium                     — provenance (upstream URL + revision)
  * LICENSE                             — the GNU LGPL v2 text

How the engine is linked
------------------------
ash-chrome (BSD-3-Clause) links this engine STATICALLY, inside the sandboxed IME
utility process, behind the ChromeOS ime mojom::InputMethod seam
(chromeos/ash/services/ime/unikey_engine.*). LGPL — unlike GPL — permits linking
the engine into a differently-licensed work; the only obligations are those of
LGPLv2 §6, discharged as follows.

The license argument, concretely
--------------------------------
1. Notices & license text: the LGPL text and upstream copyright ship here
   (LICENSE, README.chromium).
2. Complete corresponding source, with our changes: the full engine source above
   ships on every image, so any recipient has the exact source that produced the
   linked engine.
3. Means to relink a modified engine: because the engine is a self-contained
   source unit with a documented build (BUILD.gn) and no private dependencies,
   a recipient can modify these files and rebuild ash-chrome (or a standalone
   libukengine) against them to substitute their own build of the engine. The
   only Chromium-specific pieces (the mojo adapter) are BSD-3 and separately
   available. This satisfies the §6 "source form" option for relinking; the
   Chromium binary itself carries no copyleft obligation.

If Legal prefers the relink obligation quarantined to a swappable unit, the
preferred follow-up (VIETNAMESE-IME-PERF.md §3.3) is to build the engine as a
replaceable libukengine.so and dlopen it in the IME service exactly as the stock
image loads libimedecoder.so — the textbook LGPL "shared library mechanism."
This package already establishes source availability regardless of which link
form ships.

Regenerating this snapshot
--------------------------
The tarball in files/ is a pinned copy of chromium-src/src/third_party/unikey.
When that source changes, regenerate it with files/regen-snapshot.sh so the
shipped source matches the linked engine.
